  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.75$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $6$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nApproximate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=0.75$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{f}^{\u2032}(0.75)\u2248$ {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=0.75.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.25.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(0.75) & \u2248\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.75-0.25)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.5)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{0.25} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
